decisions:
  - id: D-docs-from-graph
    decision: Generate docs from scan-index rather than maintaining separate MDX documentation
    rationale: Every .purpose file already contains structured descriptions and relationships. A separate docs copy would drift. Reading the graph means docs are always current.
  - id: D-extracurricular-categories
    decision: Replace nonCredit boolean with category/track system on university content
    rationale: Categories are a proper abstraction that benefits search, onboarding, and validation. The boolean was a hack that didn't compose.
  - id: D-type-all-components
    decision: Add type fields to all 330 untyped components in a single pass
    rationale: The docs manifest groups components by type. Without types, 330 components land in an '(untyped)' bucket that makes the sidebar useless. Typing them all made the auto-generated docs immediately navigable.
  - id: D-site-reads-university-json
    decision: Site lesson pages read university course JSON at build time rather than embedding content
    rationale: Course content already exists and is maintained in the university package. Duplicating it in the site would create drift. A shared data loader reads from both packages.
  - id: D-plsat-landing-not-exam
    decision: Site PLSAT page is informational, not the actual exam
    rationale: The full PLSAT experience (timer, grading, certificates) runs in the University platform. The site page explains what it is and how to take it. Embedding the exam would require duplicating complex UI state.
learnings:
  - Component type fields have compounding value — they're marginal when adding one component but transformative when viewing the full graph as documentation
  - Unquoted YAML colons and ! prefixes are the most common .purpose file syntax errors — quoting signal keys should be documented as a convention
  - Building 1276 static pages from the symbol graph is an effective integration test for Paradigm metadata health
  - The extracurricular/core track distinction maps cleanly onto 'required for onboarding' vs 'optional enrichment' — a useful content architecture pattern
  - The site and university package have different quiz formats (choices vs options) — the data loader must normalize both
